            "result_text": "Perfect! I've created a complete git server setup with automatic web deployment. Here's what you need to do:\n\n## Quick Start\n\nOn your server, run this single command:\n\n```bash\nsudo bash complete-setup.sh\n```\n\nThis will:\n1. Install nginx\n2. Create the bare git repository at `/git/server`\n3. Install a post-receive hook for automatic deployment\n4. Configure nginx to serve on port 8080\n\n## How It Works\n\n```\ngit push origin master\n    ↓\nGit server receives push\n    ↓\npost-receive hook runs\n    ↓\nFiles automatically checked out to /var/www/html\n    ↓\nNginx serves them on port 8080\n```\n\n## Client Usage\n\nOnce the server is set up, from your local machine:\n\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server my-project\ncd my-project\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\n```\n\nThen test it:\n\n```bash\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n# Output: hello world\n```\n\n## Files Created\n\n- **complete-setup.sh** — All-in-one setup script (recommended)\n- **setup-git-server.sh** — Just the git server setup\n- **setup-nginx.sh** — Just the nginx setup\n- **nginx-config.conf** — Nginx configuration file\n- **GIT-SERVER-SETUP.md** — Detailed documentation with troubleshooting\n\nAll scripts are ready to run. Copy them to your server and execute the `complete-setup.sh` as root."
